OL,3,GNEWSANHS boss tells Eljamel inquiry: 'I
OL,4,Awon't resign over destroyed logbooks'
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe chief executive of NHS Tayside has
OL,7,Fpersonally apologised for the
OL,8,Fdestruction of theatre logbooks,
OL,9,Fpotentially related to disgraced
OL,10,Fsurgeon Sam Eljamel, but said she had
OL,11,Fno intention of resigning.
OL,13,FEljamel, who is believed to have harmed
OL,14,Fhundreds of patients, was a consultant
OL,15,Fneurosurgeon at Ninewells Hospital in
OL,16,FDundee from 1995 until his suspension
OL,17,Fin December 2013.
OL,19,FThe Eljamel public inquiry previously
OL,20,Fheard that 40 theatre logbooks were
OL,21,Fdestroyed in July 2025 despite an order
OL,22,Fnot to do so.
OL,23,APub: 09-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
